1. Introduction
In this experiment, I learned how to estimate token usage, calculate API costs and check rate limits before building an LLM-powered application. I developed a Python-based budget planner that calculates expected usage 
and checks whether a proposed feature fits within the configured limits and budget.

2. What I Did

Created a Python project for token economics and budget planning.

Used a .env file to store usage assumptions, token prices, rate limits and budget values.

Implemented budget.py to calculate daily and monthly token usage and estimated costs.

Calculated input tokens, output tokens and total tokens per day.

Implemented RPM and TPM capacity checks.

Applied a 20% safety margin to the estimated usage.

Added daily and monthly budget checks.

Created automated unit tests using Python's unittest module.

Performed what-if analysis by increasing the expected daily requests and peak requests per minute.

