5. What I Understood

Input Tokens: Tokens sent to the model, including prompts, instructions and context.

Output Tokens: Tokens generated by the model in its response.

Total Tokens: The sum of input and output tokens.

RPM (Requests Per Minute): The maximum number of requests allowed per minute.

TPM (Tokens Per Minute): The number of tokens processed per minute.

Token Pricing: The cost charged for input and output tokens, usually calculated per million tokens.

Safety Margin: Extra capacity added to handle traffic variations and estimation errors.

Budget Threshold: The maximum amount of money allowed for daily and monthly usage
